WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.644
The third gate connects the
sources, then measures how far

2
00:00:03.644 --> 00:00:07.462
the directory has drifted from
HR before anything gets fixed.

3
00:00:07.462 --> 00:00:11.713
Pull HR into SailPoint as the
authoritative source, read-only.

4
00:00:11.713 --> 00:00:14.535
Connect Entra ID through
SailPoint's connector,

5
00:00:14.535 --> 00:00:17.851
and Active Directory through
its on-premises appliance.

6
00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:20.853
In GCC High, point the Entra source at the

7
00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:24.038
US government Graph and sign-in endpoints.

8
00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:26.861
Correlate everything on the employee I D.

9
00:00:26.861 --> 00:00:31.926
Treat uncorrelated accounts as possible
orphans, not errors to suppress.

10
00:00:31.926 --> 00:00:33.840
Turn on native change detection,

11
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.237
which fires one event for each account
that changed between aggregations.

12
00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:40.824
Then run the kit's drift reconciliation.

13
00:00:40.824 --> 00:00:47.300
It joins HR, Graph and SailPoint on the
key, and reports Book 03's drift classes.

14
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.650
File that first run as the baseline.

15
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.450
And expect a burst of high-severity
findings in the first month.

16
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.630
That just means the
measurement is working.
